Z||000000||b lo 0||07-31-2000||02:12 PM||||The GT has an exhaust leak we have traced to the front manifold-missing/broken bolt.  If the bolt is just missing we just put a new one in, but if it's broken we have to take it out.  What's the easiest way to do this?  Pull the front head?  Drop the motor?  or can I use some trick and do it while it's still in there?  Please help.  Also, what bolt do I use?  There's like 6 GM bolts in the Help! section at Pep Boys.  Oh, btw, the "we" I keep referring to is me and my dad, Greg Sr.  I just wanna give him a shout and say "Thanks for helping my with my car and putting up with me for 18 years.  You're the coolest!"  I love ya, dad.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">   <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PJ||07-31-2000||09:57 PM||||If its broke off there ain't no easy way and there ain't no tricks. You can try using a right angle drill with a reverse spinning extractor bit (heating it first will help) or drill it out oversize and helicoil it. If all fails you may have to remove the head. I think the bolt is (if I remember right) an 8 x 1.25 metric. If its one of the studded bolts that also holds the manifold heat shield I can mail you one. I've got quite a few new ones. If not just get at least an 8.8 and use some anti-seize when you reinstall.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black||||reg||1
Z||000002||b lo 0||08-01-2000||10:18 AM||||Thanks PJ, I'll take a look at it this afternoon.  I may be interested in the bolt, I'll get back to you.||||reg||1
